import{_ as t,o as a,c as s,a0 as o}from"./chunks/framework.D4fUSYzX.js";const b=JSON.parse(`{"title":"ADR 0148: On the herdr-core host, the plane adopts its start into the desktop's space, not the plane's tab","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"adr/0148-on-the-herdr-core-host-the-plane-adopts-its-start-into-the-space-not-the-tab.md","filePath":"adr/0148-on-the-herdr-core-host-the-plane-adopts-its-start-into-the-space-not-the-tab.md"}`),n={name:"adr/0148-on-the-herdr-core-host-the-plane-adopts-its-start-into-the-space-not-the-tab.md"};function r(h,e,i,d,l,p){return a(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="adr-0148-on-the-herdr-core-host-the-plane-adopts-its-start-into-the-desktop-s-space-not-the-plane-s-tab" tabindex="-1">ADR 0148: On the herdr-core host, the plane adopts its start into the desktop&#39;s space, not the plane&#39;s tab <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0148-on-the-herdr-core-host-the-plane-adopts-its-start-into-the-desktop-s-space-not-the-plane-s-tab" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;ADR 0148: On the herdr-core host, the plane adopts its start into the desktop&#39;s space, not the plane&#39;s tab&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Status: accepted Date: 2026-11-13 Amends ADR 0141&#39;s Adoption label rule: the plane copies the space label its own terminal carries, and no tab label.</p><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p><a href="./0141-the-plane-resolves-its-agent-host-herdr-or-herdr-core.html">ADR 0141</a> decided that the plane copies the Adoption labels <code>herdr.space</code> and <code>herdr.tab</code> from its own herdr-core terminal onto the terminal a start takes, beside its own run labels, so the Herdr desktop shows a start the plane made the way it shows a terminal it made itself.</p><p>The live walk of 2026-11-13 measured the placement that rule produces (the machine state and the roster stand in <a href="https://github.com/SeriousJul/my-little-software-factory/blob/main/docs/verification/agent-host-herdr-core.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">the verification record</a>). The plane ran in a terminal the desktop created, and that terminal carried both labels. A Consultation the plane started that day carried both labels too, and the desktop showed it as a <strong>split pane in the plane&#39;s own tab</strong> - the Consultation beside the plane, left and right in one tab - not as a separated window of its own. The operator expected the start to stand separated, in its own tab beside the plane&#39;s.</p><p>The desktop&#39;s source settles the mechanism. The window on this machine is <code>herdr-app</code> 0.1.15. Its <code>reconcile</code> adopts every live terminal that carries a <code>herdr.space</code> label and is not already shown, and its <code>adopt</code> places it: when the terminal also carries <code>herdr.tab=&lt;id&gt;</code> and the app knows a tab by that id, the app splits the terminal <strong>into that existing tab</strong>, beside the tab&#39;s own panes; when it carries the space label alone, the app <strong>creates a tab in that space</strong> for the terminal. The desktop&#39;s own instructions state the rule: &quot;<code>herdr.tab=&lt;id&gt;</code> chooses its tab; without it, Herdr creates a tab in that space.&quot;</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>The plane copies the space label <code>herdr.space</code> from its own terminal&#39;s record, and no tab label.</strong> With the space label the start&#39;s terminal stands, when the plane stands in the desktop, as its own tab in the plane&#39;s space - separated from the plane&#39;s tab. The plane writes no label into the desktop&#39;s tab namespace at all; that label stays the desktop&#39;s own, on the terminals the desktop creates and moves. A run outside a herdr-core terminal writes no Adoption label, as before. The plane&#39;s run labels, the write-once rule, and the forensics-only roster scoping stand unchanged.</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Consequences&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>A start from a desktop terminal shows in the desktop as its own tab in the plane&#39;s space, not as a pane beside the plane in that tab. Several Consultations started from one plane stand as several tabs in that space.</li><li>ADR 0141&#39;s statement that the plane &quot;copies the Adoption labels <code>herdr.space</code> and <code>herdr.tab</code>&quot; narrows to the space label. The plane&#39;s reader of its own terminal&#39;s record still takes the record&#39;s whole label map; only the copy the start writes narrows.</li><li>The desktop&#39;s side of the new rule - a space-labeled terminal standing as its own tab in the space - is an operator read. The verification record stands it as not re-walked until the operator confirms it after this change, and a desktop that changes its adoption rule is a measured break, the way ADR 0141 stated it.</li></ul>',10)])])}const m=t(n,[["render",r]]);export{b as __pageData,m as default};
